# Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval requires a solution that improves the efficiency of its administrative services, reduces environmental footprint, and complies with regulatory requirements such as GDPR. The project has a budget of 3 million euros and a duration of four years. Key performance indicators (KPIs) include reduction in processing times, increase in the quality of answers provided by agents, and enhancement of user satisfaction.

# Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution involves the design and implementation of an intelligent assistance tool that leverages AI capabilities to accompany agents in their administrative activities. The tool will be built using large language models (LLMs) such as Mistral 7B, LLaMA 3.8B, Camembert, Falcon 7B, and fine-tuned using LoRA and QLoRA for drafting administrative contents. The solution will integrate with existing systems of information, including business software, civil status, town planning, electronic management of documents (EDM), and user directories.

From a technical perspective, our architecture proposes the use of microservices, containerization using Docker, and orchestration using Kubernetes. We will ensure high availability and scalability through the use of API gateways (Kong, Apigee, AWS API Gateway), message brokers (Apache Kafka, RabbitMQ), and monitoring tools (Prometheus, Grafana, ELK Stack).

For security compliance, we will adhere to GDPR requirements, ensuring data sovereignty hosting on SecNumCloud or equivalent infrastructure in the EU. Our solution will employ access control measures, including multi-factor authentication using Time-Based One-Time Password Algorithm (TOTP) and FIDO2 security keys, as well as role-based access control and privileged access management using CyberArk Conjur and HashiCorp Vault.

Legally, our proposal complies with GDPR, ensuring explicit validation for automated decisions and transparency in AI solutions. We will use encryption for sensitive data and adhere to the principle of data localization. Our subcontracting policy ensures that all subcontractors are EU-established and undergo a vetting process, including checks for exclusion grounds and legal and financial due diligence.

From a budgetary perspective, our contract value is 750,000 euros per year, with a target gross margin percentage of 28%. We optimize costs while ensuring high-quality service, regulatory compliance, and environmental sustainability. Our overhead costs are estimated at 145,000 euros monthly or 1,740,000 euros annually.

For AI innovation, our solution involves a phased approach, starting with a pilot phase followed by the generalization of the solution to other areas. We align with the V1 to V2 development cycle, which has a duration of nine months. Our solution is designed with explicability and transparency in mind, providing source citation, chain of thought display, and confidence scoring.

Finally, for CSR and sustainability, our proposal reduces energetic consumption and relies on infrastructures with low carbon impact. We propose several sustainability measures, including green hosting using OVHCloud and Scaleway, which provide 100% renewable energy. Our solution implements digital sobriety practices such as int8/int4 model quantization, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum five-year lifecycle.

# Unaddressed Requirements
None of the requirements specified in the tender have been left unaddressed in our proposal.

# Conclusion
In conclusion, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. and its consortium partners are confident that our proposed solution meets the City of Belval's requirements for improving administrative services efficiency while reducing environmental footprint and complying with regulatory requirements. Our comprehensive approach integrates AI, cloud architecture, security compliance, legal eligibility, budget optimization, and sustainability measures to provide a high-quality service that enhances overall efficiency and reduces costs. We look forward to the opportunity to discuss our proposal in further detail.
